# Draft: ntdll: Report individual LFH slots in heap_walk_blocks
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11502 state=opened
# HeapWalk() in Wine erroneously reports LFH (Low Fragmentation Heap) internal backing blocks as standard busy blocks (PROCESS_HEAP_ENTRY_BUSY). This causes tools relying on HeapWalk() to misreport false positive memory leaks compared to native Windows behavior. When a block has the BLOCK_FLAG_LFH flag set, it represents an LFH group rather than an ordinary user allocation. Expand active LFH groups and report all individual busy slots inside rather than grouping them, so leak detectors can track each allocation.

Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=59938

Signed-off-by: Kyle Yang kyle.chaoxin.yang@gmail.com
